function englishBriefText(){const a=allocation();return `شارعنا يستاهل — private working plan\n\nGoal: make littering socially unacceptable while making respect for public streets visible and repeatable.\nCreative approach: ${approaches[state.approach].name}. ${approaches[state.approach].note}\nOperating model: ${state.model==='independent'?'Independent organization (preferred long-term direction)':'Hosted pilot first, with a written host agreement; independent organization remains a possible destination'}.\n\nIllustrative pilot budget: ${money(state.budget)}; installed-bin assumption: ${money(state.binCost)}.\n${priorities.map((p,i)=>p.name+': '+money(a.amounts[i])).join('\n')}\n80% of physical works is reserved for bins; 20% for small improvements. Up to ${a.bins} whole installed bins cost ${money(a.spent)}; improvements: ${money(a.improvements)}; unspent bin allocation: ${money(a.remainder)}. Verify quotes and operating capacity. No donations collected here.\n\nRoadmap: Days 1–30 listen, baseline, governance, permissions and collection agreement. Days 31–60 install only where ready, launch, inspect and test. Days 61–90 compare results, repair, publish ledger, then repeat, redesign or expand one cluster.\nPlanning checklist: ${state.tasks.length}/12 complete. Placement readiness: ${state.ready.length}/5; verify each location separately.\nMeasurement: fixed-segment litter counts, usable-bin checks, pickup logs, and voluntary message recall. Proposed day-90 goals: 20% lower median litter counts; 90% usable bins and pickups. Finalize after baseline; no observed impact claimed.\n\nShortlisted messages:\n${state.saved.length?state.saved.map(k=>{const m=messageByKey(k);return `${m.audience} / ${m.tone}\n${m.line}\n${m.action}`;}).join('\n\n'):'No messages saved yet.'}\n\nBefore scale: resolve theft or overflow, confirm service funding, review tone with residents and sanitation workers, confirm the appropriate organizational/fundraising route with local advice, and keep a traceable ledger. Partnerships and celebrity roles are prospects only. The campaign is in development. This planning site is private.`;}

function englishCreatorBrief(){return `CREATIVE BRIEF — شارعنا يستاهل\n\nWe are developing an independent Egyptian anti-littering campaign. We want to make littering socially unacceptable while showing respect for people and sanitation workers.\n\nWorking direction: ${approaches[state.approach].name}.\nOne behavior: keep your litter with you until you reach a usable bin.\nCreative options: an everyday comedy sketch; an athlete carrying a bottle all the way to a bin; or a trusted presenter returning to a cared-for pilot street after 30 days.\nAsk: a short, natural Egyptian Arabic piece, one clear action, and a documented follow-up.\nBoundaries: staged or consented scenes; no public humiliation, class stereotypes, unverified impact claims, or unsafe challenges.\nAgree fees, paid-support disclosure, usage rights, return visit, and editorial approval before proceeding.\nThis is a planning draft, not an agreement or a sent outreach message.`;}
